Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:54:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10198/11362] Ratchet ARC artifact lint debt: new artifacts
 must pass, from the suite

REQ-HARNESS-5935 (spec added with this change).

THE VENUE WAS THE DEFECT. arc_artifact_lint is a pre-commit hook; result
artifacts are written once and never re-staged, and the conductor commits
with hooks skipped -- so the guard had NEVER inspected the population it
governs. Measured with the lint's own candidate selector and reproduced
before this change: 444 of 573 ARC candidate artifacts carry at least one
error (194 INVALID_INFERENCE_SUBSTRATE, 141 MISSING_INFERENCE_SUBSTRATE,
111 NON_TERMINAL_HONEST_VERDICT, 56 LIVE_LLM_NOT_ALLOWLISTED, 53
DURATION_MISSING, 18 DURATION_BELOW_SUBSTRATE_FLOOR). Note the known-issues
entry headlines 58% -- that is the substrate-only pair (335/573); the
would-fail-any-error rate is 444/573, about 78%.

Enforcement moves to where execution actually happens: pytest is the gate
the conductor runs on every task. The standing 444 are frozen behind a
baseline commit recorded in ops/arc_artifact_lint_debt_baseline.json --
a debt snapshot, not an approval; their per-class repair decision stays with
the 2026-08-28 known-issues entry. Every artifact ADDED after the baseline
commit is linted from the suite, so a task that writes a bad artifact turns
one stable, named suite node RED before that artifact is a day old, and the
REQ-HARNESS-5920 node-id delta then charges it to the run that caused it.

Fail directions, stated and pinned: a baseline commit git cannot answer for
yields None and the test FAILS -- an unmeasured population must never read
as clean (the same laundering shape closed in global_suite_baseline earlier
today). Demonstrated: the fail-open mutation (return [] on unknown commit)
passes silently on a bogus sha; the committed guard returns None and the
suite goes RED. A synthetic post-baseline artifact with an illegal substrate
is proven to draw INVALID_INFERENCE_SUBSTRATE from the exact lint call the
live test uses, so gutting the lint linkage also turns the suite RED. 4/4.

Deliberately NOT done: no entry added to SUBSTRATE_DURATION_FLOORS, no
existing gate weakened, none of the 444 relabeled -- growth stops now,
repair stays a per-class decision.

